WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.681
Module 4: the Culture Progress Monitor.

00:00:02.681 --> 00:00:07.287
After a Culture Mosaic, the client
chooses a few things to work on.

00:00:07.287 --> 00:00:11.480
Months later, someone asks the
obvious question: did it work?

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.680
The Progress Monitor answers it.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:19.317
It re-measures one to three of the Culture
Mosaic's domains and shows the baseline

00:00:19.317 --> 00:00:20.898
next to the new scores.

00:00:20.898 --> 00:00:23.510
This module takes about fifty minutes.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.791
A Progress Monitor is a progress
check, not a second Culture Mosaic.

00:00:28.791 --> 00:00:34.075
The client picks the one to three
domains they've actually been working on,

00:00:34.075 --> 00:00:36.470
and only those are measured again.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.245
Why so few?

00:00:37.245 --> 00:00:40.838
Focus: most action plans
target two or three tiles,

00:00:40.838 --> 00:00:46.545
and re-measuring all twelve invites people
to read meaning into movement on tiles

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:47.602
nobody touched.

00:00:47.602 --> 00:00:53.167
A shorter survey: fewer items means less
burden on people who already answered,

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:55.070
which helps response rates.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:58.522
And a cleaner story: "we
worked on Collaboration,

00:00:58.522 --> 00:01:02.890
and here's what changed" is
something an executive can act on.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:07.892
Leave enough time for the work to
reach people's day-to-day experience.

00:01:07.892 --> 00:01:12.542
The recommended interval is six to
nine months after the baseline.

00:01:12.542 --> 00:01:15.853
Much sooner, and you're
mostly measuring noise.

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:17.473
Here's the rule.

00:01:17.473 --> 00:01:22.451
A Progress Monitor always builds on
a Culture Mosaic run in SurveyCraft.

00:01:22.451 --> 00:01:27.083
Not an older paper survey, and not
another vendor's culture survey.

00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:31.093
The baseline must be in the
same SurveyCraft organization.

00:01:31.093 --> 00:01:34.204
It must have launched,
so not still in Draft.

00:01:34.204 --> 00:01:37.869
And it needs at least five
completed, real responses.

00:01:37.869 --> 00:01:41.740
Any number of Progress Monitors
can follow one baseline.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.819
If the client's last culture
survey was run some other way,

00:01:45.819 --> 00:01:48.654
the right first step is a Culture Mosaic.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:50.307
Let's test that.

00:01:50.307 --> 00:01:52.944
Four clients want a Progress Monitor.

00:01:52.944 --> 00:01:54.939
Only one can go ahead today.

00:01:54.939 --> 00:01:58.074
Pick it, and read why
the other three can't.

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:01.725
Pick the domains the
client actually worked on.

00:02:01.725 --> 00:02:04.077
Not the lowest scores they ignored,

00:02:04.077 --> 00:02:07.370
and not the highest scores
they hope to show off.

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:10.260
Ask which tiles their
action plan targeted.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.746
Ask what people actually experienced,

00:02:12.746 --> 00:02:18.055
because an initiative that lived only in
leadership meetings won't show up in a

00:02:18.055 --> 00:02:18.929
staff survey.

00:02:18.929 --> 00:02:21.617
And ask what they'll do with the answer.

00:02:21.617 --> 00:02:25.178
If no decision depends on
a domain, don't measure it.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:29.479
Northwind chose Collaboration,
Change Ready and Empowered Teams,

00:02:29.479 --> 00:02:31.831
its three lowest tiles in February.

00:02:31.831 --> 00:02:35.326
From April to September they
ran cross-site huddles,

00:02:35.326 --> 00:02:38.955
a joint nursing council and
a decision-rights charter,

00:02:38.955 --> 00:02:41.643
and the Progress Monitor ran in October.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:45.331
There are three ways to
order a Progress Monitor.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.745
The client can buy it on the website,

00:02:47.745 --> 00:02:51.334
signed in with the account
that ran the Culture Mosaic.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:55.575
Mosaic staff can create one for
engagements the Mosaic team runs.

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:59.164
And a coach can deploy one
from Mosaic Coaching Studio.

00:02:59.164 --> 00:03:02.491
All three apply the same
baseline and domain rules.

00:03:02.491 --> 00:03:06.994
No add-ons are sold with a Progress
Monitor, and you don't need them.

00:03:06.994 --> 00:03:11.757
Custom questions and demographic
breakdowns from the baseline come across

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:12.670
automatically.

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:14.863
Here's the website order.

00:03:14.863 --> 00:03:18.800
Sign in with the account you
ran your Culture Mosaic with.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.971
Pick the baseline from the list,

00:03:20.971 --> 00:03:26.333
which shows only eligible Culture Mosaics
with their response counts and dates.

00:03:26.333 --> 00:03:28.097
Pick one to three domains.

00:03:28.097 --> 00:03:33.594
Enter the respondent count, and a partner
code only if you're buying for your own

00:03:33.594 --> 00:03:34.205
practice.

00:03:34.205 --> 00:03:39.160
Before payment, SurveyCraft checks
that the survey can actually be built.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:42.078
Once paid, the survey
is ready immediately.

00:03:42.078 --> 00:03:45.471
Send it out exactly as you
would a Culture Mosaic,

00:03:45.471 --> 00:03:50.357
with a roster or link and reminders,
and launch within about two months.

00:03:50.357 --> 00:03:54.429
Generate the report once there
are five completed responses.

00:03:54.429 --> 00:03:59.044
If setup ever fails after payment,
the team is alerted and fixes it,

00:03:59.044 --> 00:04:00.945
and nobody has to buy again.

00:04:01.433 --> 00:04:05.937
A Progress Monitor survey is a
copy of the client's own baseline,

00:04:05.937 --> 00:04:08.016
not the master Culture Mosaic.

00:04:08.016 --> 00:04:11.758
That's deliberate: identical
wording means every item,

00:04:11.758 --> 00:04:15.361
demographic and open question
lines up across waves.

00:04:15.361 --> 00:04:20.281
It keeps the items of the domains
you chose, the demographic questions,

00:04:20.281 --> 00:04:25.201
the leader question, the open questions,
and the baseline's breakdowns,

00:04:25.201 --> 00:04:26.102
at no charge.

00:04:26.102 --> 00:04:30.814
It drops the other domains, the
safety index page and any subscales.

00:04:30.814 --> 00:04:31.645
One warning.

00:04:31.645 --> 00:04:37.120
Don't edit the demographic answer choices
between the baseline and the Progress

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:37.674
Monitor.

00:04:37.674 --> 00:04:40.723
Breakdowns are matched
by the exact wording,

00:04:40.723 --> 00:04:45.920
so if "Clinic Network" becomes "Clinics",
that breakdown can't be compared.

00:04:46.433 --> 00:04:51.478
A client can run as many Progress
Monitors as they like from one baseline,

00:04:51.478 --> 00:04:53.796
and each new report shows a trend.

00:04:53.796 --> 00:04:56.727
It starts with the
baseline Culture Mosaic,

00:04:56.727 --> 00:05:02.385
then every earlier Progress Monitor that
has five or more responses and re-measured

00:05:02.385 --> 00:05:06.339
at least one of the current
domains, then the current one.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:10.292
An earlier wave on entirely
different domains is left out.

00:05:10.292 --> 00:05:15.201
Every wave needs five or more responses
for a whole-organization report,

00:05:15.201 --> 00:05:18.200
and ten or more people
for a subteam report.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:22.699
And remember: each wave is a
different, anonymous group of people.

00:05:22.699 --> 00:05:26.244
The report compares group
averages, not individuals.

00:05:26.733 --> 00:05:30.124
Here's the shape of a
Progress Monitor report.

00:05:30.124 --> 00:05:33.737
It opens by saying what
was re-measured and when.

00:05:33.737 --> 00:05:38.528
Then comes the page most executives
go straight to: Then and Now.

00:05:38.528 --> 00:05:41.256
The baseline mosaic sits on the left,

00:05:41.256 --> 00:05:45.605
and on the right the re-measured
tiles show their new size,

00:05:45.605 --> 00:05:47.964
with everything else greyed out.

00:05:47.964 --> 00:05:51.576
Next is the progress
summary, one row per domain,

00:05:51.576 --> 00:05:56.368
showing the change in points and
a label: meaningful improvement,

00:05:56.368 --> 00:05:59.612
meaningful decline, or
no meaningful change.

00:05:59.612 --> 00:06:05.288
Meaningful means a statistical test says
the change is unlikely to be chance,

00:06:05.288 --> 00:06:07.721
and both waves had enough people.

00:06:07.721 --> 00:06:12.291
At Northwind, Collaboration rose
from forty-four to fifty-two,

00:06:12.291 --> 00:06:14.134
a meaningful improvement.

00:06:14.134 --> 00:06:19.958
Change Ready and Empowered Teams moved
a few points, with no meaningful change.

00:06:19.958 --> 00:06:24.602
After that you can drill into
each item, see progress by group,

00:06:24.602 --> 00:06:30.721
and see how the comments shifted, which
themes are new, which grew and which faded.

00:06:30.721 --> 00:06:34.112
There's no safety index
page and no subscales.

00:06:34.112 --> 00:06:36.324
It's a focused progress check.

00:06:36.833 --> 00:06:38.187
Here's another rule.

00:06:38.187 --> 00:06:42.044
Progress Monitor results never
feed any Mosaic benchmark.

00:06:42.044 --> 00:06:47.593
A progress check on a few domains, run by
an organization already working on them,

00:06:47.593 --> 00:06:50.300
isn't a fair sample of anyone's culture,

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:55.172
and adding it would distort the norms
everyone else is compared against.

00:06:55.172 --> 00:06:58.218
The report still shows
benchmark percentiles.

00:06:58.218 --> 00:07:02.616
It just never adds to them, and
there's no switch to change that.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:08.567
Time for the module check: eight
questions, and you need seven right.

00:07:08.567 --> 00:07:10.310
Retakes are unlimited.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:13.804
Here's your Progress
Monitor Setup Checklist,

00:07:13.804 --> 00:07:17.810
from "is this the right tool"
through to reading the report.

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:18.611
Download it.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:19.789
To recap.

00:07:19.789 --> 00:07:26.067
A Progress Monitor re-measures one to three
domains the client actually worked on.

00:07:26.067 --> 00:07:31.810
The baseline must be a SurveyCraft
Culture Mosaic in the same organization,

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:35.102
launched, with five or
more real responses.

00:07:35.102 --> 00:07:40.768
The survey is a copy of the baseline,
and its breakdowns come across free,

00:07:40.768 --> 00:07:43.678
with no safety index and no subscales.

00:07:43.678 --> 00:07:48.578
The trend shows the baseline,
earlier waves that share a domain,

00:07:48.578 --> 00:07:50.186
and the current wave.

00:07:50.186 --> 00:07:56.234
Change is labelled meaningful only when
a statistical test and the group floors

00:07:56.234 --> 00:07:56.694
agree.

00:07:56.694 --> 00:08:00.292
And a Progress Monitor
never joins a benchmark.

00:08:00.292 --> 00:08:03.508
Next: Module 5, the Leadership Mosaic 360.

